WEBVTT

00:01.140 --> 00:03.940
It's all over!

00:04.340 --> 00:06.500
Can't you do something
with your Teleport?

00:06.500 --> 00:10.700
My Teleport has a maximum
distance of 30 meters!

00:10.700 --> 00:14.090
At this height, it's useless!

00:15.390 --> 00:16.540
Lady Leshea!

00:16.540 --> 00:18.750
You'll be fine with this velocity, right?

00:30.260 --> 00:31.470
Ouch!

00:31.470 --> 00:32.680
Leshea!

00:35.940 --> 00:36.960
Ouch!

00:37.600 --> 00:39.600
Aww!

00:40.200 --> 00:41.330
This place...

00:41.750 --> 00:43.700
Are we on top of Uroboros' body?

00:44.750 --> 00:46.820
So the game is on, huh?

01:16.470 --> 01:24.810
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

02:18.660 --> 02:23.500
PLAYER.04: UROBOROS

02:30.550 --> 02:31.690
It's okay.

02:32.210 --> 02:34.960
Um, hello. I'm Fay.

02:34.960 --> 02:37.510
I was wondering if we could
exchange information first.

02:37.970 --> 02:40.620
We'd be happy to help, too.

02:41.060 --> 02:44.930
I'm Orvan Misketz,
the captain of Team Inferno.

02:45.830 --> 02:47.360
Long time no see.

02:47.360 --> 02:49.190
I-I'm very sorry!

02:49.510 --> 02:50.270
Yeah.

02:53.670 --> 02:55.820
Four apostles have fallen.

02:55.820 --> 02:59.830
Three of them couldn't survive the landing
and were sent back to the real world.

02:59.830 --> 03:01.420
What about the last one?

03:01.420 --> 03:03.290
It's because of them.

03:07.500 --> 03:10.170
What's that? A flying whale?!

03:10.170 --> 03:13.340
The Arcane Court calls them "Leviathans."

03:13.340 --> 03:18.140
They're waiting for humans
to fall off Uroboros' back.

03:18.840 --> 03:21.020
The moment their prey falls,

03:21.020 --> 03:24.730
they transform from whales
into ferocious piranhas.

03:24.730 --> 03:27.910
Of all the gods, we must fight
against an undefeated god...

03:27.910 --> 03:29.560
This is the worst.

03:29.560 --> 03:32.440
One more loss, and we'll be retired...

03:32.980 --> 03:37.410
Everybody, chins up!
Don't forget, we're on the stream.

03:38.660 --> 03:41.810
The whole world is watching our fight.

03:42.230 --> 03:43.910
Don't show your pitiful looks!

03:43.910 --> 03:45.570
Y-Yes, sir!

03:51.460 --> 03:53.750
Is it the meep's here?

03:53.750 --> 03:57.470
There's no point in me trying
to explain anything to you anyway.

03:57.930 --> 04:02.320
Hey, what kind of game does
Uroboros want to play with us?

04:02.320 --> 04:07.810
The "Forbidden Word." If you can get Lord
Uroboros to say a specific word, you win.

04:08.180 --> 04:10.850
What's the specific word?

04:10.850 --> 04:13.730
Finding that word
is also part of this game.

04:13.730 --> 04:16.570
By the way, the word changes every time.

04:17.060 --> 04:19.410
That sounds fun.

04:19.410 --> 04:20.620
THE FORBIDDEN WORD

04:20.620 --> 04:21.740
WIN CONDITION

04:21.740 --> 04:22.850
MAKE UROBOROS SAY XXX

04:22.850 --> 04:23.920
LOSE CONDITION

04:23.920 --> 04:24.910
ALL APOSTLES OUT

04:28.350 --> 04:30.500
Is this part of its horns?

04:32.080 --> 04:34.730
The size is almost like a building, isn't it?

04:36.530 --> 04:39.090
Uroboros' size is about 10,000 meters long.

04:39.090 --> 04:41.820
It is by far the largest god among the gods.

04:42.270 --> 04:45.720
On the search data,
the clue is in the part of its head.

04:50.900 --> 04:54.730
This is a random trap.
You have to find the forbidden word

04:54.730 --> 04:56.810
to get out of here.

04:59.080 --> 05:01.660
Sky, cloud, horns.

05:01.660 --> 05:05.030
It's supposed to be a word
that relates to this game!

05:05.700 --> 05:08.500
Scales, Leviathans, electric shock!

05:10.710 --> 05:15.920
Oh, I forgot to mention.
You all have already said the word before.

05:16.570 --> 05:18.880
That's a very important clue!

05:21.610 --> 05:23.630
Is there a time limit?!

05:24.070 --> 05:27.280
Uroboros is interfering with us.

05:27.280 --> 05:30.180
It's supposed to not be easy
to clear this up.

05:30.180 --> 05:32.400
We can't possibly guess that quickly!

05:34.160 --> 05:36.070
Horns, buildings, run!

05:36.070 --> 05:38.690
Game over, piranha, retire!

05:41.810 --> 05:42.820
"Ouch."

05:46.280 --> 05:47.990
Huh? How?

05:47.990 --> 05:49.450
I see!

05:50.960 --> 05:52.040
Ouch!

05:52.040 --> 05:54.040
Aww!

05:54.480 --> 05:56.490
The word is "ouch."

05:56.490 --> 06:00.010
Certainly, that is the only
word we uttered twice.

06:02.430 --> 06:06.930
Does this mean that if we've
found the answer, we must go?

06:16.250 --> 06:20.870
Um, can this god speak human language?

06:20.870 --> 06:23.990
First of all, it doesn't.

06:23.990 --> 06:28.220
The win condition that makes Uroboros say
"ouch" is not meant to be taken literally.

06:28.700 --> 06:29.850
For now,

06:30.630 --> 06:32.240
let's just try something.

06:32.240 --> 06:34.140
What are you going to do?

06:34.140 --> 06:37.080
I'm going to make this god scream, "Ouch!"

06:37.440 --> 06:38.470
Ouch!

06:38.470 --> 06:40.320
When you step on it,

06:40.320 --> 06:43.680
you're like an ant stamping
on the back of an elephant.

06:43.680 --> 06:45.180
Then, how about that?

06:45.590 --> 06:47.640
Let's focus all our power on one point!

06:47.960 --> 06:48.700
Yes, sir!

07:01.150 --> 07:03.240
I shot as hard as I could, but...

07:03.620 --> 07:06.410
Alright, it's my turn!

07:12.990 --> 07:15.410
Hey, Leshea! If you unleash
your power here...

07:15.410 --> 07:18.080
Here I go!

07:35.520 --> 07:38.130
I already had a bad feeling about that...

07:38.680 --> 07:40.480
Lady Leshea...

07:41.440 --> 07:44.900
I'm sorry! That was my fault!

07:45.580 --> 07:49.120
There you have it. A heartfelt apology
from the Dragon God herself.

07:49.670 --> 07:53.740
But there is no sign
of Uroboros' voice, is there?

07:54.430 --> 07:56.840
This is a game of wits.

07:56.840 --> 08:01.340
If we can't figure out how to make this god say,
"Ouch," we can't complete this game.

08:02.050 --> 08:04.840
I forgot to tell you about the hidden rules.

08:04.840 --> 08:07.550
Hidden rules?!
I didn't know about that!

08:07.550 --> 08:09.340
I'm sorry...

08:09.340 --> 08:13.510
Oh, well, that's all right.
You just told us about it.

08:13.890 --> 08:16.600
So, what are the hidden rules here?

08:16.600 --> 08:17.030
HIDDEN RULE 1

08:17.030 --> 08:20.730
HIDDEN RULE 1
If you do a certain thing, something will happen.

08:20.730 --> 08:23.550
WHEN YOU XXX
That's the first hidden rule.

08:23.550 --> 08:24.170
HIDDEN RULE 2
And when you fulfill the first hidden rule,

08:24.170 --> 08:26.520
AFTER FULFILLING HIDDEN RULE 1,
And when you fulfill the first hidden rule,

08:26.520 --> 08:30.070
YOU CAN XXX THE XXX FOR A BRIEF TIME
you can do something for a brief time.

08:30.070 --> 08:31.810
I see.

08:32.530 --> 08:36.870
Uroboros' Leviathan servants
are tracking our every move!

08:37.200 --> 08:39.260
That's because they think
we're their food.

08:39.260 --> 08:41.950
But I'm not tasty!

08:41.950 --> 08:46.480
Calm down. They only go
after us when we fall.

08:49.880 --> 08:52.060
H-Hey, Pearl...

08:52.060 --> 08:55.220
There's something a billion times scarier
than the Leviathan behind you...

08:55.720 --> 09:00.800
Hmm, so I see you're no different, Fay.

09:00.800 --> 09:03.010
Even in the ancient magical era,

09:03.010 --> 09:06.110
the sage in the kingdom once said,
"A young maiden's breasts

09:06.110 --> 09:11.820
have a charm that surpasses
even the gods' magic."

09:11.820 --> 09:13.780
Was that guy really a sage?!

09:14.250 --> 09:15.740
And you, Pearl.

09:16.460 --> 09:20.210
Weren't you going to show
your best side to them?

09:20.210 --> 09:22.720
If you spend this entire game
weeping and hiding,

09:22.720 --> 09:27.140
they'll just think,
"Oh, she's the same as ever!"

09:27.140 --> 09:29.260
T-That's...

09:31.970 --> 09:36.430
That's right. I can't be so weak
in a place like this!

09:36.770 --> 09:37.960
Will you do your best?

09:37.960 --> 09:39.270
I'll do my best!

09:39.270 --> 09:40.260
Can you run?

09:40.260 --> 09:41.440
Yes, I can!

09:41.440 --> 09:44.190
Alright, let's go searching!

09:44.190 --> 09:45.190
Yes!

09:48.540 --> 09:49.940
Good grief.

09:50.990 --> 09:53.990
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

09:57.490 --> 09:59.370
So this is the tail...

09:59.370 --> 10:01.020
Over here!

10:01.020 --> 10:04.290
Look at these spines.
They're very suspicious.

10:04.870 --> 10:09.000
You're right. The color of these
scales is very suspicious.

10:09.380 --> 10:10.840
I knew it!

10:10.840 --> 10:13.430
I've figured it out!

10:13.430 --> 10:14.090
Huh?

10:14.090 --> 10:17.220
This is a game to make
Uroboros say, "Ouch."

10:17.220 --> 10:21.200
If so, then the differently colored
scales are the vital points,

10:21.200 --> 10:24.810
and these spines are there to
ward off its enemies, namely us!

10:25.210 --> 10:28.770
Uh, Pearl, I have a bad feeling about this.
Just hold on a—

10:28.770 --> 10:31.580
In other words,
by hitting this vital point,

10:31.580 --> 10:34.660
Uroboros will scream
in pain and surrender!

10:34.660 --> 10:36.160
So it's true...

10:36.160 --> 10:38.030
She's the girl who always

10:38.030 --> 10:40.870
makes the assumption that
Ms. Miranda was talking about.

10:42.100 --> 10:44.560
Okay, let's give it a try.

10:44.960 --> 10:46.850
Pearl, attack!

10:46.850 --> 10:48.040
Leave it to me!

10:48.730 --> 10:50.050
Watch this momentous moment

10:50.050 --> 10:54.260
as I defeat the undefeated god!

10:54.260 --> 10:57.200
Ah, right.
A word of advice, just in case.

10:57.200 --> 10:59.220
Once you hit Uroboros,
you should run away.

11:00.150 --> 11:01.100
Sorry?

11:01.450 --> 11:03.430
Pearl, what are you doing?

11:03.430 --> 11:06.400
Captain Orvan, please watch this!

11:06.740 --> 11:09.360
Take this!

11:12.070 --> 11:14.780
Ah... This is about what I expected.

11:14.780 --> 11:17.110
Eh? What?

11:17.530 --> 11:22.310
Pearl, how would you feel if someone
suddenly punched you in the head?

11:22.310 --> 11:24.450
Of course, I would be angry...

11:25.600 --> 11:26.500
Watch your head!

11:34.340 --> 11:36.300
This is god's trap.

11:36.300 --> 11:39.090
Careless action only puts
the team in jeopardy.

11:41.450 --> 11:46.940
N-No, this is wrong... I'm just trying
to be helpful this time...

11:49.770 --> 11:54.240
Pearl, calm down.
I would've done it myself if you hadn't.

11:55.180 --> 11:57.110
It's an important inspection.

11:57.110 --> 12:02.080
We have to try each
and every rule and win condition.

12:02.080 --> 12:06.360
Even if I'm the one
who gets hit by that attack,

12:06.360 --> 12:08.680
I'm not going to blame you.

12:09.880 --> 12:12.010
We have to be prepared
to go through the trap.

12:12.630 --> 12:15.090
The most important promise is that

12:15.870 --> 12:18.130
you shouldn't blame your friends
who make mistakes.

12:19.570 --> 12:24.100
Captain Orvan,
you said this tail was a trap,

12:24.100 --> 12:26.450
but I don't think this god
would have any fun

12:26.450 --> 12:30.540
trapping a few humans like that.

12:31.080 --> 12:32.520
Then what?

12:32.860 --> 12:34.840
It's a proper strategy and procedure.

12:35.300 --> 12:38.470
If you attack Uroboros' tail,
it'll fight back.

12:38.470 --> 12:40.320
This is the first hidden rule.

12:40.680 --> 12:42.010
You've got to be kidding!

12:42.390 --> 12:47.200
Look at this! One wrong move,
and we would all have been annihilated!

12:47.590 --> 12:49.210
Only four apostles got annihilated.

12:49.210 --> 12:52.440
But if Uroboros had really
been out to get us,

12:52.440 --> 12:54.710
there would have been
a lot more casualties.

12:54.990 --> 13:00.010
That's right. It's strange that hundreds
of beams are hitting miss.

13:00.010 --> 13:04.330
So Uroboros made it look like a "trap"
and only hit a few people.

13:04.680 --> 13:07.620
Then what should we do next?

13:07.620 --> 13:10.900
We have to figure out
hidden rule number two.

13:10.900 --> 13:11.900
Any guesses?

13:11.900 --> 13:13.380
Not at all.

13:13.380 --> 13:15.150
How can you sound
so relaxed about it?!

13:15.550 --> 13:17.960
This is not a game
with a time limit.

13:18.340 --> 13:22.190
If we can achieve its goal,
that's all that matters.

13:26.290 --> 13:29.660
The second hidden rule is "You can do..."

13:30.340 --> 13:33.380
And it's odd that it's only
for a certain amount of time.

13:33.380 --> 13:36.740
What are the choices we haven't tried yet?

13:37.130 --> 13:38.990
It's all over!

13:38.990 --> 13:42.920
We can't figure out a single thing!
It's impossible to clear this game!

13:42.920 --> 13:48.200
As for Uroboros, the Arcane Court has also
approved 'unconditional forfeiture.'

13:48.630 --> 13:50.100
This god is a bad match for us...

13:50.640 --> 13:54.440
But there are members here
who have already lost twice.

13:54.440 --> 13:58.150
It's all because somebody
dragged us down six months ago.

13:59.890 --> 14:03.670
If we hadn't been wiped out,
we would still have had room

14:03.670 --> 14:05.450
to lose to Uroboros here!

14:07.570 --> 14:09.290
I'm sorry, I...

14:09.570 --> 14:12.830
It's your fault that
you drew Uroboros to us!

14:12.830 --> 14:16.170
Why do you even bother following us?!

14:16.170 --> 14:17.380
Silence.

14:18.300 --> 14:23.220
Is it fun for you to fool around
with this girl?

14:24.620 --> 14:28.490
You're all eyesores. If you hate being
here so much, then get out of here.

14:28.490 --> 14:32.370
I would be happy to return you
to the real world with my own hands.

14:33.270 --> 14:35.120
B-But...

14:35.120 --> 14:39.930
Isn't it unfair for a former god
to protect a person like that?

14:39.930 --> 14:43.930
It's a fact that we were all
annihilated because of her!

14:45.600 --> 14:46.640
How foolish.

14:47.640 --> 14:49.330
I've had enough.

14:49.330 --> 14:52.830
I don't have the energy to get angry
at somebody who's missing the point.

14:53.540 --> 14:57.540
This isn't about the feud between
Pearl and you. What I'm angry about...

14:58.030 --> 15:03.280
...is your attitude toward ruining this game
by bringing your emotions into it.

15:04.950 --> 15:09.180
It's such an exciting game.
Why don't you enjoy it?

15:09.590 --> 15:12.140
Exciting? That's bullshit!

15:12.140 --> 15:15.810
Who else here can say that they
haven't given up except you?!

15:16.180 --> 15:20.650
Sure, there is. I know one person
who's sincerely enjoying this game.

15:22.100 --> 15:24.740
Those beams are too powerful.

15:25.260 --> 15:27.670
Shooting those beams at a humans...

15:28.100 --> 15:30.990
If it means anything
other than overkill, then...

15:39.800 --> 15:40.840
I see!

15:42.720 --> 15:44.670
I'm going to make Uroboros angry again.

15:44.670 --> 15:45.760
Don't be a fool!

15:46.750 --> 15:49.050
It will probably cause
more casualties than before.

15:49.570 --> 15:51.190
Instead, we will win.

15:51.600 --> 15:53.270
So even if you get annihilated,

15:53.270 --> 15:56.070
I want you to see me through
to the end in the real world.

15:56.070 --> 15:57.440
What do you mean?

15:58.400 --> 16:01.900
Leshea! Punch the crap out
of that thing again!

16:02.370 --> 16:03.860
You got it!

16:32.210 --> 16:33.170
Over there!

16:37.020 --> 16:39.500
Why is the god's servant
attacking Uroboros?

16:39.500 --> 16:44.420
No one said anything about Leviathan
being Uroboros' servant.

16:44.980 --> 16:47.840
They're neutral monsters!

16:47.840 --> 16:52.160
It's not just humans who are angry
at Uroboros' attack!

17:00.330 --> 17:02.520
Uroboros is finally making a move.

17:04.840 --> 17:10.050
Did we just solve
the whole Uroboros' game?

17:10.050 --> 17:10.600
HIDDEN RULE 1

17:10.600 --> 17:13.630
WHEN YOU ATTACK UROBOROS' TAIL,
UROBOROS WILL FIGHT BACK

17:13.630 --> 17:14.500
HIDDEN RULE 2

17:14.500 --> 17:15.700
AFTER FULFILLING HIDDEN RULE 1,

17:15.700 --> 17:17.520
YOU CAN CONTROL THE LEVIATHANS FOR A BRIEF TIME
Amazing!

17:17.970 --> 17:20.980
For the first time ever,
they entered the final stage!

17:21.360 --> 17:23.310
The rest is making Uroboros say, "Ouch"!

17:23.800 --> 17:24.730
Let's go!

17:25.730 --> 17:28.390
First, we need to find
this god's real weak spot.

17:28.390 --> 17:29.820
Not the tail we attacked earlier.

17:29.820 --> 17:32.360
That means it must have
a different weak spot somewhere.

17:32.360 --> 17:33.720
Then...

17:34.150 --> 17:35.080
It's down there!

17:35.890 --> 17:37.790
Uroboros had no eyes.

17:39.410 --> 17:41.750
No, Uroboros is hiding them!

17:44.550 --> 17:47.670
We can get there only by riding Leviathans.

17:48.060 --> 17:50.130
That means...
Right here!

17:50.710 --> 17:52.760
The eyes are in this spot?!

17:52.760 --> 17:57.600
If we want Ouroboros to say "Ouch,"
we'll have to destroy its eye.

17:58.890 --> 18:00.020
Crap! Stop!

18:03.070 --> 18:04.100
Then...!

18:08.220 --> 18:11.490
Those two eyes have defense systems.

18:11.790 --> 18:13.950
Approach the right eye,
the left eye will attack,

18:14.250 --> 18:17.080
and if you approach the left eye,
the right eye will attack you.

18:17.410 --> 18:19.430
What are we going to do?

18:19.430 --> 18:21.930
We need a way to keep
the eyes from noticing us.

18:26.790 --> 18:30.010
I think we have already
run out of "brief time."

18:31.210 --> 18:32.300
Fay!

18:32.300 --> 18:33.470
I'm counting on you!

18:38.640 --> 18:40.600
Pearl, listen to me.

18:44.170 --> 18:45.520
Are you serious?!

18:45.890 --> 18:47.560
We have to do it.

18:47.560 --> 18:49.980
And we'd better do it
with perfect timing.

18:51.140 --> 18:52.070
I'll do it!

18:54.600 --> 18:56.110
This is the last one!

18:57.950 --> 18:59.580
Ascend!

19:03.460 --> 19:05.660
Pearl, I leave this to you!

19:05.660 --> 19:06.670
Yes!

19:18.800 --> 19:20.510
I got this!

19:20.510 --> 19:22.220
That's good.

19:22.650 --> 19:25.940
No holding back! Here I go!

19:34.030 --> 19:36.990
Ah, I guess I was too slow.

19:42.680 --> 19:45.370
Fay, I put a scratch on it!

19:48.840 --> 19:52.840
The gods smile at those
who make their own miracles!

19:59.090 --> 20:01.390
It's useless! The beam is faster!

20:03.790 --> 20:06.410
It's time to compare answers, Uroboros!

20:07.770 --> 20:08.730
Move me!

20:08.730 --> 20:10.310
The Wandering!

20:20.200 --> 20:22.420
'Let the god bring down the god.'

20:23.320 --> 20:28.120
This was your strategy, Uroboros.

20:39.520 --> 20:43.530
What a game...
They play the gods' game in unison.

20:44.430 --> 20:46.930
Meaning that since we were there,

20:46.930 --> 20:49.600
we're considered
to have beaten Uroboros, too.

20:50.160 --> 20:51.770
That Pearl...

20:52.730 --> 20:58.100
Folks, it seems that she has successfully
repaid her debt to us.

21:09.190 --> 21:11.000
Are you Uroboros?

21:11.940 --> 21:15.960
Well played, humans.
This time is my loss.

21:17.510 --> 21:18.920
Oh, that's right.

21:18.920 --> 21:22.140
I'll give you this.
A piece of my eye.

21:22.140 --> 21:24.930
Is that a God's Diadem?!

21:24.930 --> 21:26.180
That's right.

21:26.180 --> 21:31.550
It's a special reward for defeating
the undefeated god for the first time!

21:31.550 --> 21:34.110
Oh? What kind of effect does it have?

21:34.490 --> 21:38.570
Whenever you are carrying my eye,
you can "draw" me.

21:38.570 --> 21:43.440
I'll think of a more difficult game
next time, so let's play again.

21:46.750 --> 21:51.040
What? You're not happy? Next time,
it will be a hundred times harder.

21:51.040 --> 21:52.400
Who will do it?!

21:52.400 --> 21:53.560
I don't mind, though.

21:53.560 --> 21:57.080
Think about the difficulty level next time!
The difficulty level!

21:57.800 --> 21:58.410
VS UROBOROS, THE ENDLESS GROWTH

21:58.410 --> 22:00.450
THE FORBIDDEN WORD GAME
